# Component Development Guidelines

When developing components for @10up/block-components:

## Component Structure

- Each component should be in its own directory under `components/`
- Each component directory should include an `index.tsx` file that exports the component
- Include a `readme.md` file with documentation for the component
- Complex components can be split into multiple files within the component directory

## Component Requirements

- Components should accept well-typed props with TypeScript interfaces
- Every component should be wrapped with `StyledComponentContext` if using styled components
- Components should use the WordPress i18n functions for text
- Include namespace constants for CSS classes 
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Consider accessibility in all component designs
- Components should be tested thoroughly

## Post-related Components

- Post-related components should interact with the WordPress data store or PostContext
- Post-related components should support dynamic data retrieval
- When working with post data, use the existing PostContext where available

## Styling Components

- Use @emotion/styled for CSS-in-JS styling
- Follow WordPress design patterns where appropriate
- Maintain consistency with other WordPress admin UI elements
- When possible use components from the @wordpress/components package
- Style components to be responsive by default

